  "parent": "You are the scheduler of an evolutionary code search. Each option is one settled candidate of the population, described by its finding card (what it changed, what it hypothesised, what was observed, what it concluded, its limits) and its search score (higher is better; the baseline is the trivial predictor). The state holds the task, the population table with lineage and scores, and a knob index: for every training knob, the values already tried and by whom. Which candidate should the next job build on? Prefer a candidate whose line still has headroom on the task; avoid a line whose last change is a knob and direction the index already covers; weigh the strongest branch outside the lineage that has received the most jobs; a low-scoring candidate that carries an untried idea can be worth one job.",
  "operator": "The next job builds on the chosen parent (state.parent). Should it be an improve (one hypothesised change to the parent's code) or a crossover (combine the parent with a second candidate's idea)? Crossover is worth it when two lines hold complementary changes; improve when the parent's own line has an obvious next step.",
